# Line endings are a DETERMINISM concern in this package, not a style preference.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is set on this machine and there is no root .gitattributes,
# so without this file git would check these sources out with CRLF. Two things
# would then break, both silently:
#
#  1. print-styles.ts holds the stylesheet as a multi-line template literal, so
#     CRLF in the SOURCE puts \r\n inside the rendered HTML string itself --
#     changing the output and its sha256 between a fresh Windows clone and the
#     Ubuntu Actions runner. That is precisely the byte-for-byte approval
#     guarantee and the tailored_hash cache key (constraint #8).
#  2. The golden fixture is compared byte for byte against a freshly rendered
#     string, so a CRLF checkout fails the test on a clean clone while passing
#     for whoever generated it.
#
# eol=lf pins both to LF everywhere regardless of anyone's git config.
* text eol=lf

# The golden render is a test artifact compared byte for byte. -text disables
# ALL conversion, so it is never touched even if the rule above is relaxed.
*.golden.html -text
